erent groups of drivers for example, new drivers vs. veteran drivers. Using advanced scheduling platforms allows schedulers to easily input different driver preferences and cater to a variety of driver needs within the specific roster group, while ensuring optimized results for each group separately and across the different groups. Optibus supports the creation of rotating rosters, which create an equitable duty allocation for drivers and are simpler to maintain from the operational side. FAQ’s Your questions answered Does Optibus support complex rotation cycles and different driver groups? Yes. Optibus is built to manage the complex “human side” of operations. You can create Rota Groups for different segments of your workforce, like full-time vs. part-time, within a single project. Our roster management system supports fixed rosters, rotating cycles, and 4- or 5-day workweeks. How does the \"Rest Day\" logic work in Optibus? You can build Rest Day rosters either interactively or through full automation. The engine considers day-off patterns and guaranteed rest time as core constraints, ensuring compliance. You can also integrate stand-by duties directly into the roster to ensure you have coverage for unexpected absences. Can I modify rosters manually if I need to make a quick change? Absolutely. While our optimization engine provides a fully optimized roster, we designed the interface for “human-in-the-loop” agility. When you manually swap a duty, the system instantly re-checks all rules and preferences to ensure your change hasn’t created a compliance violation elsewhere in the cycle. How does Rostering help with the current driver shortage? Optibus allows you to create rosters that reflect actual driver preferences, like reducing split shifts or balancing overtime hours more evenly. This addresses “unbalanced” hours, ensuring drivers are not overloaded, which significantly improves long-term retention – a critical factor in solving driver shortages . Do I need to